WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.692
Sorting is useful when we want to rank values from smallest to largest or largest to smallest.

00:00:05.692 --> 00:00:08.672
NumPy can sort an array directly.

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:15.763
It can also tell us the position of the smallest or largest value using arg min and arg max.

00:00:16.341 --> 00:00:19.883
That position can be useful when the index has meaning.

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:29.128
For example, if each value represents sales for a different month, arg max can identify which month had the highest

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:29.463
sales.

00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:37.748
The distinction is important: max gives the largest value, while arg max gives the position where that value occurs.

00:00:37.748 --> 00:00:41.425
The same relationship applies to min and arg min.
